<Content
  kicker="Legal"
  title="Pricing & Fees"
  description="How avaTOK prices are shown, how tax is applied, and the fees that apply to marketplace earnings, consultations, and withdrawals."
  lead="What you pay on avaTOK, what is deducted, and where each figure is shown."
  updated="2026-08-05"
>
  <p>
    This page explains how pricing and fees work on avaTOK — our messaging, audio and video calling,
    live video calling, marketplace, and live consultancy services. It sits alongside our
    <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, <a href="/tokens">Tokens &amp; Wallet</a> policy,
    <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a> policy, and
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a> policy.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who charges you</h2>
  <p>
    Which company handles your transaction depends on where you are:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ava Global International Pvt Ltd</strong>, Mumbai, India — contracts with and serves
      customers in India, and handles India transactions and payouts under Indian law and GST.</li>
    <li><strong>Ava Global International, Inc.</strong>, Delaware, USA — contracts with and serves
      international (non-India) customers, and handles international transactions and payouts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. The screen you confirm on is the authoritative price</h2>
  <p>
    Prices, token costs, commissions, and fees are shown in the app before you confirm. Where they
    are inclusive or exclusive of tax is indicated at checkout. <strong>The figures shown on that
    screen apply to your transaction</strong> — this page describes the types of charge, not the
    amounts, because they can vary by country, currency, payment method, and listing.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Top-ups and tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Top-ups are converted into <a href="/tokens">tokens</a> at the conversion shown at the time of
    the top-up. Tokens are then used to pay for AI features, marketplace purchases, and
    consultations. The token cost of each feature or service is shown before you commit to it.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Tax</h2>
  <p>
    For customers in India, <strong>GST</strong> applies where the law requires it and is shown at
    checkout, either included in the displayed price or added on top, as indicated. For customers
    outside India, any sales tax, VAT, or equivalent that we are required to collect is shown in the
    same way.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where Indian tax law requires withholding on marketplace payouts — for example TDS — we may
    withhold the required amount from a payout. See <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a>.
    You remain responsible for your own tax position.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Platform commission on earnings</h2>
  <p>
    Where you earn on avaTOK — by selling a digital service on the marketplace or by providing a
    live consultation — we deduct a <strong>platform commission</strong> from the amount the
    customer pays. The commission applicable to a listing or booking is shown before you publish or
    accept it, and it is reflected in what is credited to your balance.
  </p>
  <p>
    Commission is separate from the withdrawal transfer fee. Earnings are credited to your token
    balance; moving that balance to your bank is a withdrawal.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Withdrawal transfer fee</h2>
  <p>
    Withdrawing unused tokens is subject to a <strong>transfer fee</strong>, plus GST where it
    applies in India. Both are shown at the time of withdrawal, before you confirm. Your own bank or
    payment provider may apply its own charge on top, which we do not control. Full detail is on the
    <a href="/payouts">Payouts &amp; Withdrawals</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>7. App-store fees</h2>
  <p>
    Where you buy through the Android or iOS app, the purchase is processed by <strong>Google
    Play</strong> or <strong>Apple</strong> and their commercial terms apply to that transaction.
    The price you see in the store is the price you pay; store commission is deducted from what
    reaches us, not added to your bill. Refunds for those purchases are handled by the store — see
    <a href="/refunds">Refunds &amp; Cancellations</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Currency and conversion</h2>
  <p>
    Prices are normally shown in <strong>INR</strong> for customers in India and in
    <strong>USD</strong> or another supported currency for international customers. If your payment
    method is in a different currency from the one you are charged in, your bank, card issuer, or
    app store may apply its own conversion rate and a foreign-transaction fee. Those are set by them
    and are outside our control, so the amount on your statement may differ slightly from the amount
    shown in the app.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Where each charge appears</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Charge</th><th>Where it is shown</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Top-up amount and tokens received</td><td>The top-up screen, before you pay</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Token cost of a feature or booking</td><td>Before you confirm the action</td></tr>
      <tr><td>GST or other tax</td><td>At checkout, marked inclusive or exclusive</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Platform commission on earnings</td><td>On the listing or booking, before you accept</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Withdrawal transfer fee and tax</td><td>On the withdrawal screen, before you confirm</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Tax withheld on a payout</td><td>On the payout record</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>10. Changes to pricing</h2>
  <p>
    We may change prices, token costs, commissions, and fees. Where a change affects you, we will
    give notice — in the app, by email, or by updating this page — before it takes effect, as far as
    is reasonably practicable. Continuing to use a paid feature after a change takes effect means
    the new pricing applies to you. A change does not retroactively alter a transaction you have
    already completed.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this page from time to time. We will post the updated version here and revise the
    "Last updated" date above.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Billing, pricing, and payout questions:
